# 020 LED chaser (docs/machines/020-led-chaser/LED_CHASER.md): a 16-bit divider of four 74LS161
# makes STEP (about 15.3 Hz); the 74LS164 U5 shifts one low bit along S1–S8, and the 8-input
# NAND U6 feeds a new low bit into SER each time S1–S7 are all high. LEDs D1–D8 sink into S1–S8
# through R2–R9, so each is lit while its stage is low.

part X1 OSC freq=1MHz
part J1 POWER
part R1 R value=4k7
part R2 R value=330
part R3 R value=330
part R4 R value=330
part R5 R value=330
part R6 R value=330
part R7 R value=330
part R8 R value=330
part R9 R value=330
part U1 74LS161
part U2 74LS161
part U3 74LS161
part U4 74LS161
part U5 74LS164
part U6 74LS30
part D1 LED
part D2 LED
part D3 LED
part D4 LED
part D5 LED
part D6 LED
part D7 LED
part D8 LED

net CLK      X1.OUT U1.CLK U2.CLK U3.CLK U4.CLK
net RESET_N  R1.2 U1.CLR_N U2.CLR_N U3.CLR_N U4.CLR_N U5.CLR_N
net VCC      R1.1 R2.1 R3.1 R4.1 R5.1 R6.1 R7.1 R8.1 R9.1

# Every counter always counts and never loads; U1 is the low nibble, enabled for good.
net VCC      U1.ENP U1.LOAD_N U2.ENP U2.LOAD_N U3.ENP U3.LOAD_N U4.ENP U4.LOAD_N
net VCC      U1.ENT
net GND      U1.A U1.B U1.C U1.D U2.A U2.B U2.C U2.D U3.A U3.B U3.C U3.D
net GND      U4.A U4.B U4.C U4.D

net C0       U1.QA
net C1       U1.QB
net C2       U1.QC
net C3       U1.QD
net CARRY1   U1.RCO U2.ENT
net C4       U2.QA
net C5       U2.QB
net C6       U2.QC
net C7       U2.QD
net CARRY2   U2.RCO U3.ENT
net C8       U3.QA
net C9       U3.QB
net C10      U3.QC
net C11      U3.QD
net CARRY3   U3.RCO U4.ENT
net C12      U4.QA
net C13      U4.QB
net C14      U4.QC
net STEP     U4.QD U5.CLK

# Shift register: B tied high, so A (SER) is the serial input; the NAND's eighth input is tied
# high, so SER is low only while S1–S7 are all high.
net VCC      U5.B U6.H
net SER      U6.Y U5.A
net S1       U5.QA U6.A D1.K
net S2       U5.QB U6.B D2.K
net S3       U5.QC U6.C D3.K
net S4       U5.QD U6.D D4.K
net S5       U5.QE U6.E D5.K
net S6       U5.QF U6.F D6.K
net S7       U5.QG U6.G D7.K
net S8       U5.QH D8.K

# LEDs: +5 V through R2–R9 into the anodes; the cathodes sink into S1–S8.
net LED_A1   R2.2 D1.A
net LED_A2   R3.2 D2.A
net LED_A3   R4.2 D3.A
net LED_A4   R5.2 D4.A
net LED_A5   R6.2 D5.A
net LED_A6   R7.2 D6.A
net LED_A7   R8.2 D7.A
net LED_A8   R9.2 D8.A
